WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.420
How many sounds are there in a quiet backyard?

2
00:00:03.640 --> 00:00:06.340
Most of the time we hear without really listening.

3
00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:10.860
Two still minutes and a sheet of paper let your child find out.

4
00:00:13.833 --> 00:00:18.793
In about thirty minutes, your child sits still, counts sounds, and draws a map of

5
00:00:18.793 --> 00:00:21.553
them. Then they test their own ears.

6
00:00:22.893 --> 00:00:27.293
Your child practices listening closely, sorting what they hear, and checking a

7
00:00:27.293 --> 00:00:28.293
guess.

8
00:00:28.617 --> 00:00:32.697
Gather paper, crayons, a clipboard or book, a timer, and a mat.

9
00:00:34.017 --> 00:00:38.757
Pick a spot you have permission to use, away from roads, driveways, ponds, and

10
00:00:38.757 --> 00:00:41.737
streams. Stay close enough to touch.

11
00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:46.800
Ask first, 'How many different sounds do you think we will hear in two minutes?'

12
00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:48.340
Write the number down.

13
00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:50.500
Then set the timer.

14
00:00:51.740 --> 00:00:55.820
Your child closes their eyes and holds up one finger for each new sound.

15
00:00:56.933 --> 00:01:00.873
When the timer ends, ask, 'Was it more or fewer than you thought?'

16
00:01:02.013 --> 00:01:06.593
Expect anything from a few sounds to a dozen or more, depending on the place and

17
00:01:06.593 --> 00:01:07.593
time of day.

18
00:01:08.317 --> 00:01:09.637
Now the sound map.

19
00:01:10.937 --> 00:01:13.637
Put a dot in the middle of the paper and label it 'me'.

20
00:01:14.937 --> 00:01:18.037
Your child draws each sound in the direction it came from.

21
00:01:19.437 --> 00:01:22.497
Near sounds go close to the dot, far sounds near the edge.

22
00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:25.170
Add one rule at a time.

23
00:01:26.650 --> 00:01:29.250
Loud sounds are drawn big, and soft sounds small.

24
00:01:30.430 --> 00:01:32.670
High and low are a different thing, called pitch.

25
00:01:34.070 --> 00:01:37.230
Add an arrow up for a high sound, and down for a low one.

26
00:01:38.183 --> 00:01:43.603
Last, circle the sounds made by living things, like birds, insects, dogs, and

27
00:01:43.603 --> 00:01:46.463
people. Talk about the tricky ones.

28
00:01:47.663 --> 00:01:51.083
Rustling leaves come from a tree, but the wind makes them move.

29
00:01:52.167 --> 00:01:54.047
Choose a quiet, steady sound.

30
00:01:55.327 --> 00:01:59.047
Use a guarded fan on a stable surface with its cord tucked away.

31
00:02:00.307 --> 00:02:02.507
Sit your child at least an arm's length back.

32
00:02:03.747 --> 00:02:05.467
Have them face the sound and listen.

33
00:02:06.787 --> 00:02:09.287
Then have them cup their hands, fingers together.

34
00:02:10.417 --> 00:02:11.877
A question for you.

35
00:02:12.957 --> 00:02:16.477
Your child keeps the hands cupped, then turns their back to the fan.

36
00:02:17.817 --> 00:02:20.537
Will the sound get louder, fainter, or stay the same?

37
00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:28.780
Most children hear it louder with hands cupped.

38
00:02:29.860 --> 00:02:32.240
Have them turn around with their hands still cupped.

39
00:02:33.380 --> 00:02:34.820
It usually sounds fainter.

40
00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:38.620
The bigger funnels now face away from the sound.

41
00:02:39.650 --> 00:02:43.450
Cats and horses have large ears they can turn toward a sound.

42
00:02:44.850 --> 00:02:47.430
Ask, 'What do you think a cat's big ears help it do?'

43
00:02:48.070 --> 00:02:51.110
Watch only a pet your child knows, and stay beside them.

44
00:02:52.050 --> 00:02:54.330
Stay close enough to touch the whole time.

45
00:02:55.690 --> 00:02:59.470
Cup hands only for quiet, everyday sounds, never toward a road.

46
00:03:00.650 --> 00:03:02.630
If something loud starts, move away.

47
00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:05.310
Nothing goes into the ear.

48
00:03:06.333 --> 00:03:08.533
Nothing from the ground goes in mouths.

49
00:03:10.013 --> 00:03:13.893
Small objects like pebbles and acorns can choke children under four.

50
00:03:15.233 --> 00:03:17.213
Call nine one one if a child is choking.

51
00:03:18.553 --> 00:03:21.413
Never taste wild plants, berries, or mushrooms.

52
00:03:22.793 --> 00:03:24.413
Wash hands after touching them.

53
00:03:25.533 --> 00:03:27.333
Check for ticks after sitting in grass.

54
00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:31.340
Ask what your child noticed when they cupped their hands.

55
00:03:32.560 --> 00:03:35.840
Look back at the map together and trace where the sounds came from.
